  "trusted_assumptions": "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, official scalar models and Lean kernel are trusted. Wrapping, casts, shifts and rotations in the primary proofs use official models, not Rust std body proofs. Range proofs instead include the original std wrapping_neg bodies transparently, with no new provider or model. Lean dependency audits permit only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.\n\nThe four supplemental Into/TryInto body specializations additionally trust a default-off finite export patch that emits exactly the original transparent core bodies and omits duplicate rust_fun registrations. It changes no body, type, callback or Std model. Original source/LLBC, patch/binary hashes, default-off comparison and enabled export guards are retained; no general translator equivalence is established.\n\nKani results trust Kani/CBMC, the pinned August Rust compiler and solver semantics. Float composition uses the identical Rust helper across two universal specifications; no general Aeneas floating-point model or mechanized cross-tool equivalence is asserted. Exact compiler-commit standard sources show Any uses a TypeId intrinsic. Sized CloneToUninit has a clone/write default and a TrivialClone nonoverlapping-copy specialization, which may apply to these Clone+Copy types; the fixed-slot result does not prove arbitrary pointer validity or a particular dispatch route.",
